{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_405dd5ac50134c4080727d66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything works. Key findings:\n\n1. `{a,..}` → exactly ONE request, path `/api/v1/files/{a,..}` — Go's server accepted it. ✓\n2. `x[1-2].md` → ONE request, path `/api/v1/files/x[1-2].md` ✓\n3. `25 Tasks/x y.md` → `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md` ✓\n4. vault-list `* Tasks/*.md` → rawquery `glob=%2a+Tasks%2f%2a.md`. \n\nImportant: the raw query is `glob=%2a+Tasks%2f%2a.md`. `r.URL.RawQuery` is the raw escaped form. `r.URL.Query().Get(\"glob\")` would decode to `* Tasks/*.md`. \n\nRequirement 10 says: \"`* Tasks/*.md` → the recorded `glob` query parameter equals `* Tasks/*.md`\". So I need the *decoded* value. `url.ParseQuery(r.URL.RawQuery).Get(\"glob\")` → `* Tasks/*.md`. Let me record both raw query and decoded param value.\n\nHmm — `%2a` decodes to `*`, `+` decodes to space. Yes → `* Tasks/*.md`. ✓\n\nSo my recorder should record the raw query AND the decoded parameter. Let me store `query url.Values` (decoded). But `url.Values` is a map — copying is fine.\n\nRequirement 9 says \"records method, raw request path and raw query\". I'll record: method, requestURI, path (raw escaped path), rawQuery, and decoded query values. That's a superset and lets me assert both.\n\nAlso note: for `prometheus`, rawquery = `query=up` — good, and decoded `query` = `up`.\n\nLet me also check the truncation and HTTP error cases with the probe. And also verify the max-time. Let me do a quick additional probe for 500/401 and truncation.\n\nActually I'm fairly confident. But let me verify the truncation path exits 0 and outputs exactly 65536 bytes — worth checking since `head -c` on a pipe... no, it's a file.\n\nLet me quickly probe those too.\n\nActually, let me just write the real test suite now and run it — that's the real verification. But a quick probe of truncation is cheap and de-risks. Let me do it.\n\nLet me now write the test files.\n\nTest file design:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage scripts_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"net/http/httptest\"\n\t\"net/url\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tmaxBodyBytes = 65536\n\tscriptTimeout = 10 * time.Second\n)\n\n// recordedRequest is one request the recording server observed.\ntype recordedRequest struct {\n\tmethod     string\n\trequestURI string\n\tpath       string\n\trawQuery   string\n\tquery      url.Values\n}\n\n// recorder collects the requests a test server observed. Safe for concurrent use.\ntype recorder struct {\n\tmu       sync.Mutex\n\trequests []recordedRequest\n}\n\nfunc (r *recorder) record(request recordedRequest) {\n\tr.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer r.mu.Unlock()\n\tr.requests = append(r.requests, request)\n}\n\n// all returns a copy of the recorded requests.\nfunc (r *recorder) all() []recordedRequest {\n\tr.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer r.mu.Unlock()\n\tout := make([]recordedRequest, len(r.requests))\n\tcopy(out, r.requests)\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// count returns how many requests the server observed.\nfunc (r *recorder) count() int {\n\tr.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer r.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn len(r.requests)\n}\n\n// newRecordingServer starts a test server answering every request with the given\n// status and body, and records what it received.\nfunc newRecordingServer(status int, body string) (*httptest.Server, *recorder) {\n\trec := &recorder{}\n\tserver := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\trec.record(recordedRequest{\n\t\t\tmethod:     r.Method,\n\t\t\trequestURI: r.RequestURI,\n\t\t\tpath:       rawPath(r.RequestURI),\n\t\t\trawQuery:   r.URL.RawQuery,\n\t\t\tquery:      r.URL.Query(),\n\t\t})\n\t\tw.WriteHeader(status)\n\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(body))\n\t}))\n\tDeferCleanup(server.Close)\n\treturn server, rec\n}\n\n// rawPath returns the escaped request path of a request URI, without its query.\nfunc rawPath(requestURI string) string {\n\tif index := strings.Index(requestURI, \"?\"); index >= 0 {\n\t\treturn requestURI[:index]\n\t}\n\treturn requestURI\n}\n\n// scriptPath resolves a script name to its absolute path in the repository.\nfunc scriptPath(name string) string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(repoRoot(), \"agent\", \"scripts\", name)\n}\n\n// runScript executes the real script through the real subprocess boundary. The\n// child environment is built explicitly: the ambient proxy variables would\n// otherwise route a loopback request to the proxy and the recording server\n// would observe nothing.\nfunc runScript(script string, env map[string]string, args ...string) (string, string, int) {\n\thome, err := os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"observation-scripts-home-\")\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tDeferCleanup(func() { _ = os.RemoveAll(home) })\n\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), scriptTimeout)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath(script), args...)\n\tcmd.Env = []string{\"PATH=\" + os.Getenv(\"PATH\"), \"HOME=\" + home}\n\tfor key, value := range env {\n\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, key+\"=\"+value)\n\t}\n\n\tvar stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = &stdout\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\n\trunErr := cmd.Run()\n\tif runErr == nil {\n\t\treturn stdout.String(), stderr.String(), 0\n\t}\n\n\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n\tif !errors.As(runErr, &exitErr) {\n\t\tFail(\"run \" + script + \": \" + runErr.Error())\n\t}\n\treturn stdout.String(), stderr.String(), exitErr.ExitCode()\n}\n```\n\nWait — `exec.CommandContext` with gosec G204. Let me check whether the standalone gosec flags it. I'll test.\n\nThen assertion helpers:\n\n```go\n// expectRejected asserts the script refused the arguments with exit 2 and made no request.\nfunc expectRejected(script string, env map[string]string, rec *recorder, args ...string) {\n\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runScript(script, env, args...)\n\tExpect(exitCode).To(Equal(2))\n\tExpect(stdout).To(BeEmpty())\n\tExpect(stderr).NotTo(BeEmpty())\n\tExpect(rec.count()).To(Equal(0))\n}\n\n// expectUsageError asserts the script refused the argument count with exit 2 and made no request.\nfunc expectUsageError(script string, env map[string]string, rec *recorder, args ...string) {\n\t...same...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, these two are identical. Just use one: `expectRefused`.\n\n```go\n// expectRefused asserts the script exited 2, wrote a reason to stderr, and made no request.\nfunc expectRefused(script string, env map[string]string, rec *recorder, args ...string) {\n\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runScript(script, env, args...)\n\tExpect(exitCode).To(Equal(2))\n\tExpect(stdout).To(BeEmpty())\n\tExpect(stderr).NotTo(BeEmpty())\n\tExpect(rec.count()).To(Equal(0))\n}\n```\n\n```go\n// expectMissingEnv asserts the script named the missing endpoint variable on stderr.\nfunc expectMissingEnv(script string, variable string, args ...string) {\n\t_, stderr, exitCode := runScript(script, map[string]string{}, args...)\n\tExpect(exitCode).NotTo(Equal(0))\n\tExpect(stderr).To(ContainSubstring(variable))\n}\n```\n\n```go\n// expectHTTPError asserts a non-200 response surfaces the status on stderr.\nfunc expectHTTPError(script string, env map[string]string, status int, args ...string) {\n\tserver, rec := newRecordingServer(status, \"ignored\")\n\t... \n}\n```\n\nHmm, that mixes server creation. Let me instead make the It bodies do it with a DescribeTable:\n\n```go\nDescribeTable(\"surfaces the HTTP status on stderr\",\n\tfunc(status int) {\n\t\tserver, rec := newRecordingServer(status, \"ignored\")\n\t\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runScript(script, endpointEnv(server.URL), \"up\")\n\t\tExpect(exitCode).NotTo(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(stdout).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\tExpect(stderr).To(ContainSubstring(strconv.Itoa(status)))\n\t\tExpect(rec.count()).To(Equal(1))\n\t},\n\tEntry(\"server error\", http.StatusInternalServerError),\n\tEntry(\"unauthorized\", http.StatusUnauthorized),\n)\n```\n\nwhere `endpointEnv` is per-script. Let me just inline `map[string]string{\"PROMETHEUS_URL\": server.URL}`.\n\nAnd truncation helper:\n```go\n// expectTruncated asserts a body over the cap is cut to exactly maxBodyBytes and still succeeds.\nfunc expectTruncated(script string, env map[string]string, args ...string) {\n\tserver, _ := newRecordingServer(http.StatusOK, strings.Repeat(\"a\", 100*1024))\n\t...\n}\n```\nHmm, the env needs the server URL which is created inside. Let me pass the env-var name instead:\n\n```go\nfunc expectTruncated(script string, endpointVar string, args ...string) {\n\tserver, _ := newRecordingServer(http.StatusOK, strings.Repeat(\"a\", 100*1024))\n\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runScript(script, map[string]string{endpointVar: server.URL}, args...)\n\tExpect(exitCode).To(Equal(0))\n\tExpect(stdout).To(HaveLen(maxBodyBytes))\n\tExpect(stderr).To(ContainSubstring(\"truncated\"))\n}\n```\n\nAnd `assertReadOnly`:\n```go\n// assertReadOnly asserts every recorded request is a GET under the given raw path prefix.\nfunc assertReadOnly(rec *recorder, pathPrefix string) {\n\trequests := rec.all()\n\tExpect(requests).NotTo(BeEmpty())\n\tfor _, request := range requests {\n\t\tExpect(request.method).To(Equal(http.MethodGet))\n\t\tExpect(request.path).To(HavePrefix(pathPrefix))\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNow the specs.\n\nPrometheus describe:\n\n```go\nvar _ = Describe(\"prometheus-query.sh\", func() {\n\tconst script = \"prometheus-query.sh\"\n\n\tIt(\"sends one GET to the fixed query endpoint with the expression\", func() {\n\t\tserver, rec := newRecordingServer(http.StatusOK, `{\"status\":\"success\"}`)\n\t\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runScript(\n\t\t\tscript,\n\t\t\tmap[string]string{\"PROMETHEUS_URL\": server.URL},\n\t\t\t\"up\",\n\t\